The '''1996 United States Senate election in Oregon''' was held on November 5, 1996. Incumbent [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] [[United States Senator]] [[Mark Hatfield]] decided to retire after thirty years in the Senate. [[Oregon State Senate]] [[List of Presidents of the Oregon State Senate|President]] [[Gordon H. Smith]], who had run for the Senate [[1996 United States Senate special election in Oregon|earlier that year]], won the Republican primary, while businessman [[Tom Bruggere]] won a contested [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] primary. The contest between Smith and Bruggere was one of the toughest that year, but ultimately, Smith was able to keep the seat in the Republican column and defeated Bruggere by a narrow margin. This is the last time that Oregon simultaneously voted for presidential and U.S. Senate candidates of different political parties.

==Democratic primary==
===Candidates===
* [[Tom Bruggere]], businessman
* Bill Dwyer, State Senator
* [[Harry Lonsdale]], businessman and nominee for the U.S. Senate [[1990 United States Senate election in Oregon|in 1990]]
* Anna Nevenich, nurse and perennial candidate
* [[Jerry Rust]], [[Lane County, Oregon|Lane County]] Commissioner and candidate for [[Governor of Oregon]] in [[1982 Oregon gubernatorial election|1982]]

